"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThere were several ways to get to The Gap Park, and we decided to take the ferry.\n\nWhen we arrived at the ferry dock, we heard that light snacks were allowed on board,  \nso we grabbed some bread and coffee to go from a nearby cafe.\n\nThe coffee came out quickly after ordering, and the bread was warmed up right away.  \nThe coffee was decent, and the bread was better than expected.\n\nIt was convenient — just tap your transit card and board.  \nIt seemed like the ferry was just everyday public transport for locals, which I envied.\n\nOnce on board, everyone headed up to the deck, so we tried to follow,  \nbut it was too crowded and the crew told us to come back down as the ferry was departing, so we came back down.\n\nStill, we found a spot with a great view and enjoyed our coffee and bread at a leisurely pace.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n"